    draft capture pass `max_query_len`; the Ascend override left it
    unbounded (`num_tokens`), diverging from upstream for mixed FULL graphs
    | Forward `max_query_len=desc.max_query_len or desc.uniform_token_count`
    on main |
    | `vllm_ascend/worker/v2/spec_decode/dflash/aclgraph.py` |
    [vllm#57632](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57632) added a
    trailing `precompute_context_kv` to `DFlashCudaGraphManager.capture`, so
    the Ascend override's positional `super().capture()` call shifts |
    Version-split `capture`, accepting and forwarding
    `precompute_context_kv` on main (passed by keyword) |
    
    > **Notes**
    > - `hidden_out` is an accidental empty file introduced by a shell
    redirect in `fe6d042a0`; remove it before merging.
    > - The branch commits `cacf5b7d5` (`model_runner_v1.py` routed-experts)
    and `f763bc65e` (workflow edits) were reverted later in the branch, so
    they do not appear in the net PR diff and are omitted.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
